{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"7d2888eb5ed3dce9455e1a5c5de750e08ee013018d281166d10d57e34ecdfa1c","digest":{"component_or_area":"fetcher pagination","key_entities":["fetcher._iter_pages","fetcher.collect","fetcher.py:324-326","get_parent_map","SilentTruncationError","jira.search.views.default.max","startAt","maxResults","page_size"],"problem_keywords":["pagination truncation","inbound snapshot loss","silent data loss","page termination","offset truncation"],"propositions":["_iter_pages terminates on a short page and advances by the requested page_size instead of the actual page length, causing truncated pages to be misinterpreted as the end of results","when a Jira server caps pages below the requested size (e.g., default max of 20 vs requested 100), the pager exits prematurely and silently loses 92% of issues from the inbound snapshot","the same truncation defect was previously fixed in get_parent_map but remains unfixed in _iter_pages, the shared inbound path affecting both Cloud and Data Center bridges","termination logic must advance by len(page) and terminate only on empty pages, with a guard against offset-stall loops where servers ignore startAt and return the same full page repeatedly"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787463997888780001,"uuid":"17a9fba7-c512-4340-9584-de3c904c76e0"}